# Workspace packages whose test suite `.github/scripts/run-package-suites.sh`
# does NOT run. One package per line, `<name>  # reason`, and the reason is
# mandatory — the script rejects a bare name.
#
# Only two reasons qualify:
#
#   1. Another workflow already runs the same suite. Running it twice buys
#      nothing and doubles the surface a flake can land on.
#   2. It cannot produce a result on this runner at any exit code — it needs the
#      app up, a provider API key, or a browser. A suite like that would spend
#      minutes failing on purpose, which is not a signal, it is a bill.
#
# "It is red today" is NOT one of them. That goes in
# .github/package-suites.allowed-failures, which still RUNS the suite, so the
# day it goes green the job says so.
#
# A line naming a package the workspace no longer has fails the job. That is the
# only automatic pressure on this file, and it is deliberate: nothing mechanical
# can tell a justified exclusion from a capitulation, so the reason column is
# what a reviewer reads.

@langwatch/web  # this workflow's own test-unit, test-component and test-integration jobs are its suite
langwatch  # sdk-javascript-ci.yml runs the TypeScript SDK's suite
@langwatch/mcp-server  # mcp-javascript-ci.yml runs it
@langwatch/agent-plugin  # agent-plugin-ci.yml runs it
langwatch-e2e-tests  # e2e-ci.yml runs it, against an app it starts first; Playwright against nothing is 30 failed connection attempts
